I would like to ask a question related to animal radio-tracking studies.
We radiotracked the amphibian (Less movement) once every three hours.
There are many samples with no movement (distance = 0m).
For example, there are 500 samples and 450 data with 0 values.
In this case, I think the bias will be severe.
I would like to hear advice or comments on this
if there is a previous study on this question, I would be grateful if you give me the title.

